# Popular Egotist ({2}{B}) T1, with a Memnite, a Lotus Petal and three Moxen in play. T3: Bad Moon (an enchantment) is cast and then
# sacrificed to {1}{B} (Mox Jet, Mox Pearl: the pool is spent exactly): the Egotist gains indestructible and taps (CR 702.12b), and the
# sacrifice drains Bot2 for 1 (CR 603.10a), resolving before the ability does (CR 608.1, the trigger is put on the stack above it).
# Sacrificing a Lotus Petal for mana (an artifact, not a creature or enchantment) drains again. T5: with only the Egotist and a
# Memnite as creatures, the Memnite is the one that can be sacrificed to the ability (a creature: third drain); then, with {1}{B} untapped
# and no other creature or enchantment but the Egotist itself, it cannot be activated.

